//BUG="FEEDBACK.md 1.16 — an indentation jump of several levels is accepted"
//ERR any
//MSG="Indentation"

// parse_indentation_block treats any increase in indentation as exactly one
// new block, so jumping from 0 to 8 spaces silently opens a single nested
// block instead of being reported. In a language where indentation is the
// block structure, a two-level jump is almost always a typo, and accepting it
// means the mistake shows up later as a confusing type error — or not at all.
//
// Once this is diagnosed, replace `//ERR any` with the exact span.

fn main
        out "ok"
